  "memory_candidates": [
    {
      "content": "When migrating a large batch of files to a new sanctioned commit pattern, use EXPLICIT FILE-LIST pathspecs for the migration task's own commits, never a directory-level pathspec (e.g. 'agent-system/extensions/lean/'), even when every file in that directory was intentionally touched. A directory pathspec silently sweeps in any OTHER pre-existing uncommitted change under that directory (e.g. an unrelated index-entries.json numeric field bump from a concurrent process), which is exactly the over-staging defect a scoped-commit migration is meant to fix. Caught mid-task in this repo (task 48/scoped-commit migration): Phase 7's own commit swept in an unrelated lean/index-entries.json change via a directory pathspec; every phase commit from Phase 8 onward switched to explicit file lists.",
      "category": "PATTERN",
