      ]
    },
    {
      "content": "A cross-repo command/skill (one that operates on a DIFFERENT repo than its own source store, e.g. via a $TARGET_ROOT, $GLOBAL_ROOT, or $CSLIB_DIR variable) should invoke that OTHER repo's own deployed .claude/scripts/<script>.sh by absolute or relative path (e.g. bash \"${TARGET_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/git-commit-scoped.sh\") rather than the locally-resolved script. git-commit-scoped.sh (and similarly-designed scripts) derive PROJECT_ROOT from their OWN script location via common_repo_root and cd there internally, so invoking the target repo's copy automatically operates in the right repo with no separate `cd` needed -- this pattern was applied at skill-meta/SKILL.md, meta-builder-agent.md, and two sites in cslib/commands/pr.md during task 48's scoped-commit migration.",
